    defer calling ffi.cstr_free with (transmute c_text to ref to char)
    return calling raygui.GuiCheckBox with bounds, c_text, checked

## Draws a combo box; the list itself is drawn by `dropdown_box`.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `bounds`: the widget's rectangle in screen coordinates
## - `text`: the entries, in raygui's semicolon-separated format
## - `active`: the selected entry
##
## ## Returns
## raygui's widget state as an `int`: measured, `0` is idle and `1` is the press or change signal, so a click test is `state == 1`. The wrapper does not translate it into a `bool` because raygui distinguishes more states than two.
##
## ## Notes
## raygui splits the collapsed box and the open list into two widgets, and they must share the same `active` index.
##
## ## Memory
## Each PenguScript string is copied into a C string that the wrapper frees before returning; raygui keeps nothing.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling rayguix.combo_box with bounds, "640x480;800x600", (sigil of choice)
## ```

weave combo_box with bounds as raylib.Rectangle, text as string, active as ref to int into int:
    let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
    defer calling ffi.cstr_free with (transmute c_text to ref to char)
    return calling raygui.GuiComboBox with bounds, c_text, active

## Draws the open list part of a combo box.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `bounds`: the widget's rectangle in screen coordinates
## - `text`: the entries, in raygui's semicolon-separated format
## - `active`: the selected entry
## - `edit_mode`: whether the list is open
##
## ## Returns
## raygui's widget state as an `int`: measured, `0` is idle and `1` is the press or change signal, so a click test is `state == 1`. The wrapper does not translate it into a `bool` because raygui distinguishes more states than two.
##
## ## Notes
## Pass the same `active` you gave `combo_box`, and flip `edit_mode` when the combo reports a click, which is the standard raygui dance.
##
## ## Memory
## Each PenguScript string is copied into a C string that the wrapper frees before returning; raygui keeps nothing.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## calling rayguix.dropdown_box with bounds, "640x480;800x600", (sigil of choice), open
## ```

weave dropdown_box with bounds as raylib.Rectangle, text as string, active as ref to int, edit_mode as bool into int:
    let c_text as ref to frozen char is calling ffi.cstr_from_string with text
    defer calling ffi.cstr_free with (transmute c_text to ref to char)
    return calling raygui.GuiDropdownBox with bounds, c_text, active, edit_mode

## Draws a numeric spinner with increment buttons.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `bounds`: the widget's rectangle in screen coordinates
## - `text`: the label raygui draws inside the widget
## - `value`: the number, read and written
## - `min_value`: the lowest allowed value
## - `max_value`: the highest allowed value
