    return calling raygui.GuiMessageBox with bounds, c_title, c_message, c_button_text, button_active

## Draws an editable text field and hands the edited text back.
##
## ## Parameters
## - `bounds`: the widget's rectangle in screen coordinates
## - `text`: the text, seeded into the field and replaced by what comes back
## - `capacity`: the field's buffer size in bytes; typing past it truncates
## - `edit_mode`: whether the field is being typed into
##
## ## Returns
## raygui's widget state as an `int`: measured, `0` is idle and `1` is the press or change signal, so a click test is `state == 1`. The wrapper does not translate it into a `bool` because raygui distinguishes more states than two.
##
## ## Notes
## **This is the family's design centre.** raygui edits a caller-owned C buffer in place, and PenguScript strings are immutable, so the wrapper allocates the buffer, seeds it with your text, calls raygui and copies the result back into the `ref to string` you passed.
## `capacity` is the buffer's size: raygui writes as the user types, so it must be larger than the text that goes in. raygui respects the size it is given, so a long edit truncates instead of overflowing.
## The copy is byte by byte, because PenguScript has no `memcpy`, no pointer arithmetic and no assignable slice view.
##
## ## Memory
## The wrapper owns the C buffer and frees it; the caller's `string` is replaced by an owned copy of the edited text.
##
## ## Example
## ```pengu
## var state as int is calling rayguix.text_box with bounds, (sigil of text), 128, editing
## ```

weave text_box with bounds as raylib.Rectangle, text as ref to string, capacity as int, edit_mode as bool into int:
    let raw as ref to void is calling raylib.MemAlloc with (capacity to u32)
    defer calling raylib.MemFree with raw
    var buffer as slice of byte is calling ffi.slice_of_bytes_from_ptr with raw, capacity
    calling _seed_buffer with buffer, (essence of text), capacity
    var state as int is calling raygui.GuiTextBox with bounds, (transmute raw to ref to char), capacity, edit_mode
    set essence of text is (calling _read_buffer with buffer)
    return state

## Draws an editable numeric field for a float.
